"""
JUKEBOX v0.5.0 - build hook.  Writes jukebox_pkg.vhd next to this file.  Pure python (the builder runs it
with the system interpreter).

The look is fitted to the photo (WIN_20230315_00_28_42): a grid of tall rainbow capsules.

  vertical    d = |y - row centre| (triangle, period 520 lines = 2.077 rows per frame, centres on line
              259.45 + 520 k); dn = d / 260.  V(dn) = 0.0078 + 3.6254 dn + 1.7107 dn^2 (fold units),
              minus a seam dip 0.768 * clip(1 - 31.48 (1 - dn)) (G; R sees 0.35 of it).
  horizontal  a 2-column oscillator (period 419.8 px = 4.574 per 1920; columns 9.15 across); every
              column starts with a reset transient.  Column tables T[type][pos] (type 0 = the narrow
              red-topped B column of the photo, 1 = the A column; pos 0..255 across the column) hold
              the measured waveforms the oscillator feeds the three colour channels:
                E   G-field offset (Q8 fold units)      a  G vertical gain (Q7)
                c   G contrast (Q7)                     o  G mean offset (Q8)
                r   R offset (levels)                   bo B offset - 184 (levels)
                bg  B vertical gain (Q7)
  colour      G = 10 + 233 (o + c tri(a Bands (V + etch luma) + E + t))      (tri = triangle fold, period 2)
              R = r + 36.5 (Vr + tint) - 0.0898 G
              B = 184 + bo - 79 bg (V - tint) - 0.0859 G
              then BT.601 to 10-bit YUV in the hardware convention (U register = Cr, V = Cb), luma
              pre-scaled 16/13 against the output conditioning's 13/16.

Package contents:
  C_JB_T0..T3   512 x 16 column tables, address = type & pos:
                T0 = E (12, signed) & "0000",  T1 = a & c,  T2 = o (signed) & bg,  T3 = r & bo.
  C_JB_RGB_R/G/B 256 x 32 colour matrix ROMs: {y contribution (10, unsigned), u (10, signed), v (10,
                signed), 00} of one channel's 8-bit level.
  C_JB_NOSE     64 x 8: nose stretch s (Q6) = 64 * 2^((512 - 16 k) / 300), k = K3 >> 4.
"""
